## 4.2 SOCIAL DOMAIN

### 4.2.1 `posts`

Purpose: Stores user-created text content.

Proposed fields:

- id
- author_id
- content
- visibility
- is_anonymous
- community_id, nullable
- status
- created_at
- updated_at
- deleted_at, nullable

Rules:

- Author identity must remain internally available for safety and enforcement.
- Anonymous posting only changes public attribution.
- Anonymous status must never allow an unauthenticated post to bypass user ownership.
- Post content must be validated server-side.
- Removed or deleted posts must follow the approved retention model.
- Moderation must be able to suppress content without erasing audit history.

Suggested statuses:

- published
- hidden
- removed
- deleted

### 4.2.2 `post_reactions`

Purpose: Stores user reactions to posts.

Proposed fields:

- id
- post_id
- user_id
- reaction_type
- created_at
- updated_at

Approved reaction types:

- like
- funny
- interesting
- surprising

Constraints:

- One active reaction per user per post.
- Reaction type must be one of the approved values.
- Post and user must exist.

A database unique constraint must prevent duplicate reactions.

### 4.2.3 `comments`

Purpose: Stores text comments associated with posts.

Proposed fields:

- id
- post_id
- author_id
- content
- status
- created_at
- updated_at
- deleted_at, nullable

Rules:

- Comments must belong to valid posts.
- Author ownership must be enforced.
- Comment content must be validated.
- Deleted or moderated comments must follow the approved retention policy.

Nested replies are not assumed in the MVP. Do not introduce recursive comment relationships without approval.

