# 13. BACKUP AND RECOVERY

## 13.1 Backup requirements

Production database backups must be configured and monitored.

Document:

- Backup method.
- Backup frequency.
- Retention.
- Encryption.
- Access controls.
- Recovery point objective (RPO).
- Recovery time objective (RTO).

The actual RPO and RTO must be approved according to business and infrastructure requirements (TBD — owner Dennis; see README Open Decisions register). Backup frequency and retention are likewise TBD; do not invent them.

## 13.2 Restore testing

A backup is not considered verified until restoration has been tested.

Test:

- Full database restoration.
- Schema integrity.
- Foreign-key integrity.
- RLS and permissions.
- Application connectivity.
- Representative user workflows.

## 13.3 Migration recovery

For each production migration, define whether recovery requires:

- Reversal.
- Forward fix.
- Point-in-time recovery.
- Data repair.

Do not automatically reverse a migration if doing so would discard valid new user data.

